=46irst: thanks for the nice new features all the time (I hope full XEN=20
support will be in-kernel soon).

I currently run a 2.6.26.3 kernel which works (on the machine I type=20
this e-mail). I tried 2.6.27-rc4, works too. But -rc5 does not even=20
boot, and I have no idea how to produce a log of what's happening as it=20
doesn't even find the disks.

As far as I could read on screen, there are some "PCI INT A" not=20
resettable for AHCI-SATA, and all the USB drivers do NOT load as it=20
cannot reset the controller. So even my keyboard does not work, as it's=20
USB.

The mainboard is an ABIT AX78, with an AMD Phenom(tm) 9850 Quad-Core=20
Processor, 8GB RAM. I attach a bit of hardware info (lspci, lsmod,=20
kernel-config files from 2.6.26.3 and .27-rc5), so maybe somebody finds=20
it useful.

In case of questions please contact me directly, I am not on this list.

mfg zmi
